  "description": "link.v1 §2.2, §2.7: one resource's kind token, template and resolved annotations, and the face's expose -> its exposure and whether its pushes cross. token is the resource's kind token (stream, @stream, state, @state, events, @op); template is its template text; annotations are its resolved annotations (core §9.3), of which only link.exposure is read; expose is the face policy's link or none. expect.exposure is host (absent, or \"host\"), link (\"link\"), invalid (any other value), or ignored (an operation, whatever the value). expect.pushes is downsampled, whole, denied, or none (an operation has no pushes). expect.reason is the first of these that holds, in this order: requests_only (an operation); invalid; host; face_closed (the face exposes none); templated (a stream or @stream whose template has a parameter); exposed."
